From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:07:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: Say who pinned a message, not the message again
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A pin in Discord came to the Messaging app as the pinned message
written again after a "📌", as a new message from its author, at the
time of the pin: the gateway's MESSAGE_UPDATE with "pinned" true was
taken as a pin and the whole message shown once more. An edit of a
pinned message came the same way, as a new "📌" message instead of
the edit.

A MESSAGE_UPDATE is now only ever an edit, which changes the stored
message in place as any other edit does, or nothing: a pin or an unpin
changes no text. Who pinned what comes from Discord as its own message,
MESSAGE_CHANNEL_PINNED_MESSAGE, with no content and the pinned message
in message_reference. In a group DM or a server channel that is now a
line, as a group DM's rename or someone added is: "ann pinned a
message", or "You pinned a message", as tdlib-purple says a Telegram
pin. The line has no sender, so the app draws it as the service's own
and raises no notification, and it carries the pinned message as its
quote, as a reply does, so the app shows which message it was and a
tap on the quote goes to it. A server channel that is not open is not
opened for it; the line is written from its history once it is.

Discord itself says nothing of an unpin, and neither does this. A pin
in a one-to-one DM is not written: the transport keeps no line without
a sender there, as for Telegram's.

tests/test_group_rename.c checks the pin line in a group and in a
server channel (the server's name for who pinned), by the user, with a
name to escape, the quoted message from message_reference or
referenced_message, written once when replayed, a group not open
opened for it, a server channel not open left alone and written later,
nothing for a one-to-one DM, and that a reply quotes nothing.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
---
